    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The Scala driver builds on the MongoDB Java Reactive Streams driver; its `Observable` extends `Publisher` and adds convenience methods for processing operation results. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/scala/scala-driver/current/crud/query/observables.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c3b74b2a5d86861d93323a158af0186a29458982f42192e247eef18ec953d7fd",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:928a10fe0eb8d7e4db626a95f7e50b2b802506ab8c4077a10eb20c61d50b1178"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Calling `subscribe()` with an `Observer` requests operation results; `FindObservable[T]`, `DistinctObservable[T]`, and `AggregateObservable[T]` also support operation-specific configuration before subscription. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/scala/scala-driver/current/crud/query/observables.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c3057141087dcb9cb57e9f2f66bbddbf23d7b4a2aaccc7c39f5dc0d82528d0d2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:f239df1e31a6abec3953ef99ac9116b1178882e5228f9503c15326524920367d"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "An `Observer` receives results through `onNext`, terminal failures through `onError`, and completion through `onComplete`; subscription overloads also accept lambda callbacks. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/scala/scala-driver/current/crud/query/observables.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:2b4d41331cc2968e4c3e387e63dd00632eb66477e4e3f619d8dd578e2ecaf468",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
